// Which calls lead into another process: the edge from a function that
// starts a spawn, a task or an agent to what that process runs. A walk
// over what one process runs (reach.dl's SameProcess variants, calls.dl's
// waits) stops at these edges.
//
// Apart from the points-to stage (points_to.dl) and read there too: it
// is derived from the start sites and the call graph alone, so an
// analysis that walks a process's own calls does not wait for, or read,
// the process points-to.
//
// Prerequisites: include clientlib/imports.dl before this file.

// `func`'s edge to `callee` leads into another process: callee is what a
// spawn, a task or an agent in func runs, and func does not call it
// itself. A closure or fun reference of func's is set aside too when it
// is func's only one and func starts a process on a fun points-to does
// not follow (the fun came from a variable, or a helper spawns its
// parameter) or a child whose spec may hold a fun: with one there is
// nothing to confuse the handed one with. A function with several keeps them all:
// which one is handed off is not known, and one handed to Enum.each
// runs in the caller's process. A closure handed to Task.async_stream is
// not set aside either: the caller waits for what it does. Told without
// closure_def (by the compiler's name for a closure), which the
// supervision family must not read (stage0_test).
.decl runs_elsewhere(func: symbol, callee: symbol)

runs_elsewhere(f, g) :-
  process_start(_, f, _, kind, g),
  kind != "server",
  !call_instr(f, g, _),
  !calls_fun(f).

// A function that calls a fun value may run the one it starts inline as
// well (`worker = fn -> ... end`, then a task or `worker.()`, which the
// compiler makes a call to the closure when it can: call_instr).
.decl calls_fun(func: symbol)

calls_fun(f) :- dynamic_call(_, f, "call_fun").

runs_elsewhere(f, g) :-
  hands_funs_off(f),
  closure_edge(f, g),
  closure_edges(f, 1),
  !call_instr(f, g, _).

.decl closure_edge(func: symbol, closure: symbol)

closure_edge(f, g) :-
  hands_funs_off(f),
  call_edge(f, g),
  (match(".*:-.*-fun-[0-9]+-/[0-9]+", g) ; fun_ref(f, g)).

.decl closure_edges(func: symbol, n: number)

closure_edges(f, n) :-
  closure_edge(f, _),
  n = count : { closure_edge(f, _) }.

.decl hands_funs_off(func: symbol)

hands_funs_off(f) :- process_start(_, f, _, kind, "dynamic"), kind != "server".

// `start_worker(fn -> ... end)`: the start is a helper's, on its
// parameter.
hands_funs_off(f) :-
  call_edge(f, h),
  process_start(_, h, _, kind, "dynamic"),
  kind != "server".

// A child spec built around a fun (`start: {Task, :start_link, [fn ->
// ... end]}`) runs it in the child.
hands_funs_off(f) :-
  call_site(_, f, m, "start_child", _),
  (m = "Supervisor" ; m = "DynamicSupervisor").
